    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460-a2">

                <pb facs="0772" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg638"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    628.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Count Bismarck to Mr. Coleman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-06-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 16,
                    1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned has had the honor to receive the esteemed note of to-day, in
                    which Mr. Coleman conveys the expression of the sympathy of the President of the
                    United States and of the American people in the death of His Majesty the late
                    Emperor Frederick.</p>
                <p>The undersigned has not failed to communicate to His Majesty the ruling Emperor
                    the warm words in which were clothed the sentiments of the President and his
                    Government for the Imperial family and the German people.</p>
                <p>While the undersigned at the same time permits himself to cordially thank the
                    chargé d’affaires for the expression of his personal sentiments, he avails,
                    etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Bismarck.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
